{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_f179ee57-479d-49a1-ba0d-69f034ae1290","role":"user","created":1775332763,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_8e0e1a84f6ba4e6097e7a18b","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3103:Table IFS-1 shows the reserve assets of the United States, including its gold stock, special drawing rights held in the Special Drawing Account in the International Monetary Fund, holdings of convertible foreign currencies, and reserve position in the International Monetary Fund.\n3105:Table IFS-2 brings together statistics on liabilities to foreign official institutions, and selected liabilities to all\n3109:Table IFS-3 shows U.S. Treasury nonmarketable bonds and notes issued to official institutions and other residents of foreign countries.\n3111:Table IFS-4 presents a measure of the general foreign exchange value of the U.S. dollar.\n3113:Table IFS-1. - U.S. Reserve Assets [In millions of dollars]\n3146:Table IFS-2. - Selected U.S. Liabilities to Foreigners\n3173:Footnote 12, Table IFS-2.\n3183:Table IFS-3. - Nonmarketable U.S. Treasury Bonds and Notes Issued to Official Institutions and Other Residents of Foreign Countries\n3219:Table IFS-4.--Trade-Weighted Index of Foreign Currency Value of the Dollar","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"3103:Table IFS-1 shows the reserve assets of the United States, including its gold stock, special drawing rights held in the Special Drawing Account in the International Monetary Fund, holdings of convertible foreign currencies, and reserve position in the International Monetary Fund.\n3105:Table IFS-2 brings together statistics on liabilities to foreign official institutions, and selected liabilities to all\n3109:Table IFS-3 shows U.S. Treasury nonmarketable bonds and notes issued to official institutions and other residents of foreign countries.\n3111:Table IFS-4 presents a measure of the general foreign exchange value of the U.S. dollar.\